  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">On mutual consent (Govt and UNDP) agreed to work in 15 major components to take forward the scheme. we are in the process of inviting and shortlisting proposals to shortlist right agency to implement theses 15 components as per UNDP direction.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">No district has formed skill committees as on date
No District Skill development plan prepared for now or if prepared at the draft stage. 
Not much awareness is given about the initiative across the state. 
District Employment offices are functional but need to upgrade them into skill exchange centres</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Institutional strengthening at the state, district and block levels by planning, delivering and monitoring awareness creation and information dissemination on skill development initiatives of the State Government.
2. Institutional Strengthening in the state of Uttarakhand by brining in convergence, quality improvement and better monitoring and evaluation.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-10 District Level Capacity Building workshops for 268 District Level Government officials, skill development ecosystem officials, training providers were conducted.
-87 Block Level Capacity Building workshops were conducted for capacitating 2132 Block level stakeholders including block level government officials, NGOs, Gram Panchayat members and other stakeholders
-8 Bank Linkage workshops for 296 Stake holders including bank officials, small and medium level entrepreneurs and self-employment aspirants were conducted across the State.
-Training of 205 participants (Rag Pickers) through mobile van.
- Development of a biometric attendance app and mobile application for ITIs.
- Development of course content and curriculum for the popular /State specific courses, in collaboration with Tourism and Hospitality Skill Council. 
- Hiring of PR Agency done. 
- Several Workshops held with industry associations and sector skill councils pertaining to the toruism and hospitality sector, rubber and petrochemicals skill council etc. 
- Organised a State Level exhibition of Traditional handicrafts and folk art.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 1.1 Recruitment of DRPs 
A 1.2 Recruitment of SRP
A 2.1 Centre Inspection and Bio-metric application 
A 3.1 Impact Evaluation
B 3.1 District Level activities and workshops
B 3.3 PR Agency
and other 9 RFPs to be floated and recruited.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities A 1.1 and A 1.2 achieved 
A 1.1 Recruiting DRPs (District Resource Persons) in 13 districts of the state (6 On boarded and others are yet to join by mid of september 2021)
A 1.2 Recruiting SRP (State Resource Person) to support state skill development office has been onboarded.

Advertisement is made for 2 proposals 
A 3.1 Impact Evaluation
B 3.3 PR Agency

Received proposals for both. 
Review and evaluation is completed. 

Final decision to shortlist the same is awaiting with scores in hand. 

Working on the below ToR for calling proposals
A 2.1 Centre Inspection and Bio-metric application 
B 3.1 District Level activities and workshops</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
